audit_conclusions:
- Slice C is input plumbing only.
- OrchestratorRouteContextPacket enters Gemini Orchestrator input only under explicit gate.
- The new packet input gate alone does not start Gemini.
- Existing Gemini Orchestrator mode without the new gate is unchanged.
- OrchestratorRouteContextPacket is validated before provider dispatch.
- Validation failure blocks provider before model/network/Gemini call.
- allowed_routes is consistent with Orchestrator proposal contract: proof_full_pipeline.
- source_runtime_route remains metadata only.
- route_source remains metadata only.
- ContextPacket is not truth.
- ContextPacket is not authority.
- ContextPacket is not action permission.
- ContextPacket is not FinalOutput.
- ContextPacket is not ActionCommitPacket.
- Orchestrator is not Root.
- Orchestrator does not create ActionCommitPacket.
- Orchestrator does not call connectors.
- Gemini proposes, Root disposes.
- Root remains final authority.
- Dual Gemini path still passes and Architect consumes validated route as before.
- No raw cross-role text.
- No default output shape drift.
- No counter drift.
- No stage_map drift.
- No production/public WOW claim.
- No NeedleFactory/Marennya/UP.
- Ready for Slice D only after this audit is committed.

verdict:
- Rich Context / Bounded Context Packets Slice C accepted as gated Gemini Orchestrator input plumbing.
- The packet input preserves Root authority and leaves downstream Architect, PlanGraph, AVF, DRS, GT/LGT, and Root behavior unchanged.
- Root remains final authority.
